title: Heartland Concordat
subtitle: The Heartland government has reached an agreement with the Vatican.
view-if: year = 1929 and month = 7 and heartland_leader != "Bristol" and marcher_heartland and heartland_concordat = 0
max-visits: 1
tags: event
new-page: true

= Heartland Concordat

Despite our Otto Bristol losing his position as the Minister-President of Heartland, he still possesses great influence within state politics and together with <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> members, have negotiated a concordat with the Vatican. 

- @sign_concordat: The Heartland government shall sign the concordat.

@sign_concordat
on-arrival: heartland_concordat = 1; unionist_relation += 4; faithful_marcher += 3*(1-dissent); faithful_traditionalist -= 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; ddp_relation -= 2; ddp_cohesion -= 0.5; lvp_relation -= 2

We have signed a Concordat between the Free State of Heartland and the Roman Catholic Church, guaranteeing religious freedom for Catholics in Heartland. This sets the stage for the negotiation of a national Concordat covering all of the Commonwealth.

[? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": The Catholic members of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> in Heartland are in open conflict with their leadership over the vote, with many leaving the party. ?]
